<title>GERMANY: German Jan-Sept aluminium/copper/zinc output rises.</title>
<headline>German Jan-Sept aluminium/copper/zinc output rises.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>German output of primary aluminium, copper and zinc in January/September 1996 was above year-ago levels, monthly data from the state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Primary lead output in January/September extended its losses over 1995. But losses in semi-finished metals output in the nine months narrowed further, pointing to improved processing activity.</p>
<p>Aluminium castings output also rose more strongly than in January/August and lead castings maintained a strong advantage over last year, but others remained weak.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes--</p>
<p> METALS OUTPUT	   Sept 96   Jan/Sept 96	 pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/Sept 95</p>
<p> primary aluminium     47,080     431,536		 +  0.9</p>
<p> electrolytic copper   48,493     443,622		 + 12.1</p>
<p> zinc			27,555     246,192		 +  2.4</p>
<p> refined lead	    18,529     129,618		 - 26.6</p>
<p> SEMI-FINISHED METALS  Sept 96   Jan/Sept 96	  pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/Sept 95</p>
<p> aluminium		130,185   1,173,046		 -  5.3</p>
<p> copper		   132,275   1,085,059		 -  7.1</p>
<p> zinc			17,151     128,893		 +  3.1</p>
<p> lead			 4,909	34,864		 - 15.9</p>
<p> nickel		     1,346	13,213		 +  1.5</p>
<p> METALS CASTINGS	 Sept 96   Jan/Sept 96	  pct change</p>
<p>							   over Jan/Sept 95</p>
<p> aluminium		 40,475     357,884		 +  1.0</p>
<p> copper		     6,160	53,346		 - 17.9</p>
<p> zinc			 5,256	47,707		 - 12.5</p>
<p> lead			   494	 4,860		 + 41.2</p>
<p> tin			     20	   171		 - 14.1</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures include alloys. Nickel castings data were not given.</p>
<p>-- Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
